 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "V_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The pilot, Agustin Alvarez of Vigo, was a former Spanish amateur boxer (Guardian: 'former Spanish amateur boxing champion'; Chilevision/Gestion: 'ex boxeador espanol'); with two Ecuadorian crewmates he crossed the Atlantic in a homemade fibreglass semi-submersible. Narration: 'A boxer sailed a homemade sub across the Atlantic.' (headline: AN AMATEUR BOXER)",
   "sources": [
    "guardian22",
    "chv",
    "gestion",
    "elind22"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_coke",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "It carried about 3,000 kg of cocaine (AEAT: about 3,000 kg in 152 bales; Guardian: 3,068 kg; El Independiente: over 3,000 kg). Narration: 'With 3,000 kilos of cocaine on board.'",
   "sources": [
    "aeat",
    "interior",
    "guardian22",
    "elind22"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_days",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The voyage lasted 27 days (about 3,500 miles), from the Amazon (a clandestine shipyard in Brazil) to Galicia. Narration: 'How long at sea? Twenty-seven days, from Brazil's Amazon.' (early 2019 reports via El Pais said built in Guyana / sailed from Colombia; the trial-era accounts say a shipyard in the Brazilian Amazon)",
   "sources": [
    "guardian22",
    "elind22",
    "chv",
    "mdz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_tip",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The Maritime Analysis and Operations Centre (MAOC-N, Lisbon) warned that a suspicious vessel loaded with cocaine would head to Spain across the Atlantic; the operation was run by the Agencia Tributaria, Guardia Civil and Policia Nacional. Narration: 'But police were warned.'",
   "sources": [
    "aeat",
    "interior",
    "moncloa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_first",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT CARD: it was the first narco-submarine detected / intercepted in Europe. Narration: 'Europe's first narco-sub was coming.'",
   "sources": [
    "aeat",
    "interior",
    "occrp",
    "insight"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_sank",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In bad weather, unable to transfer the cargo, the crew tried to sink (scuttled) the craft near the shore at the mouth of the Aldan estuary, Cangas (Pontevedra), on 24 November 2019; the two Ecuadorians were arrested; the craft was taken to the port of Aldan. Narration: 'So the crew sank their own sub.'",
   "sources": [
    "aeat",
    "occrp",
    "guardian22",
    "janes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_wetsuit",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The third crew member (the Spanish pilot) escaped the operation, stayed hidden and was arrested on Friday 29 November 2019 (five days later), still wearing his wetsuit. Narration: 'But the boxer got away. Five days later, the police found him. He was still wearing his wetsuit.'",
   "sources": [
    "elind19",
    "guardian19"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_value",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "reported",
   "text": "STATISTIC (counter): officials put the cargo's value at about 100 million euros. Narration: 'Officials put the cargo at 100 million euros.'",
   "sources": [
    "thelocal",
    "malaymail"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_lesson",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "LESSON CARD (practical, for the viewer): UK Border Force warns that gangs target school and university leavers and first-time travellers with 'free' trips to recruit drug couriers. Its tips: refuse 'free' holidays, flights or luxury accommodation ('if it sounds too good to be true, it probably is'); know what is in your bag and never travel with a bag that is not yours. Rows: \"A 'FREE' TRIP OR FLIGHT\", 'A BAG THAT IS NOT YOURS', 'TOO GOOD TO BE TRUE'.",
   "sources": [
    "borderforce",
    "v2radio",
    "stratford"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "V_sentence",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "In 2022 the Audiencia Provincial de Pontevedra sentenced all three crew members to 11 years in prison (for the two Ecuadorians, 8 years served then expulsion); the Galician High Court (TSXG) confirmed the 11-year terms. Narration: 'Their sentence? Eleven years each. Twenty-seven days at sea. Eleven years inside.'",
   "sources": [
    "guardian22",
    "tsxg",
    "vigoe_tsxg",
    "eldiarioec"
   ]
  }
 ],
